 "scribe_vocals_2": {
  "text": "Motion. Motion. Change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line. Common to everything in the universe. Motion. Motion. We walk, we ride a bicycle, we run. Sleeping, air moves into and out of our lungs. Blood flows in arteries and veins. Carry people, automobiles, and planes. Water flowing down a dam, leaves falling from trees. Earth rotates once every twenty-four hours. Revolves round the sun once in a year. The sun in motion in the Milky Way, Milky Way. Moving within its local group of galaxies. Rectilinear motion, uniform acceleration. A set of simple equations. Relative nature of motion, relative velocity. Point objects valid so far as size is much smaller than the distance it moves in a reasonable duration of time. Real life, good number of situations. Size neglected without much error. Motion. Motion. Change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line.",
