 "sarvam_vocals": {
  "text": "Motion. Motion. Change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line. Common to everything in the universe. Motion! Motion! We walk, we ride a bicycle, we run. Sleeping, air moves into and out of our lungs. Blood flows in arteries and veins. Carry people, automobiles and planes. Water flowing down a dam, leaves falling from trees. Earth rotates once every 24 hours, revolves around the sun once in a year. The sun in motion in the Milky Way, Milky Way moving within its local group of galaxies, Rec. To linear motion, uniform acceleration, a set of simple equations, relative nature of motion, relative velocity. Point objects valid so far as size is much smaller than the distance it moves in a reasonable duration of time. Real life, good number of situations, size neglected without much error. Motion, motion, change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration, along a straight line.",
